       aarrcchh (string, default to compiled in value)
              Same  as the --AA option to Amd.  Allows you to override the value
              of the _a_r_c_h Amd variable.


       aauuttoo__aattttrrccaacchhee (numeric, default=0)
              Specify in seconds (or units of 0.1 seconds,  depending  on  the
              OS),  what  is the (kernel‐side) NFS attribute cache timeout for
              @i{Amd}’s own automount points.  A value of  0  is  supposed  to
              turn  off  attribute  caching, meaning that @i{Amd} will be con‐
              sulted via a kernel‐RPC each time  someone  stat()’s  the  mount
              point  (which  could  be  abused as a denial‐of‐service attack).
              Warning: some OSs are incapable of turning off the NFS attribute
              cache reliably.  On such systems, Amd may not work reliably  un‐
              der  heavy  load.   See the README.attrcache document in the Am‐
              utils distribution for more details.


       aauuttoo__ddiirr (string, default=/a)
              Same as the --aa option to Amd.  This sets the  private  directory
              where Amd will create sub‐directories for its real mount points.


       ccaacchhee__dduurraattiioonn (numeric, default=300)
              Same as the --cc option to Amd.  Sets the duration in seconds that
              looked‐up or mounted map entries remain in the cache.


       cclluusstteerr (string, default no cluster)
              Same  as  the  --CC  option to Amd.  Specifies the alternate HP‐UX
              cluster to use.


       ddeebbuugg__mmttaabb__ffiillee (string, default=/tmp/mnttab)
              Path to mtab file that is used by Amd to store a list of mounted
              file systems during debug‐mtab mode.  This option  only  applies
              to systems that store mtab information on disk.

       ddeebbuugg__ooppttiioonnss (string, default no debug options)
              Same as the --DD option to Amd.  Specify any debugging options for
              Amd.   Works only if am‐utils was configured for debugging using
              the ‐‐enable‐debug option.  The "mem" option,  as  well  as  all
              other  options, can be turned on via ‐‐enable‐debug=mem.  Other‐
              wise debugging options are ignored.  Options  are  comma  delim‐
              ited,  and  can  be  preceded by the string "no" to negate their
              meaning.  You can get the list of supported debugging options by
              running Amd -H.  Possible values are:

              aallll       all options (excludes hrtime and mtab)
              ddeeffaauullttss  "sensible" default options (all‐‐excluding hrtime, mtab, and xdrtrace)
              tteesstt      full debug options plus mtab,nodaemon,nofork,noamq
              aammqq       register for amq
              ddaaeemmoonn    enter daemon mode
              ffoorrkk      fork server
              ffuullll      program trace
              hhrrttiimmee    print high resolution time stamps (only if syslog(3) is not used)
              iinnffoo      info service specific debugging (hesiod, nis, etc.)
              mmeemm       trace memory allocations
              mmttaabb      use local "/tmp/mtab" file
              rreeaaddddiirr   show browsable_dirs progress
              ssttrr       debug string munging
              ttrraaccee     trace protocol and NFS mount arguments
              xxddrrttrraaccee  trace XDR routines


       ddiissmmoouunntt__iinntteerrvvaall (numeric, default=120)
              Same as the --ww option to Amd.  Specify in seconds, the time  be‐
